1. Scope

"Licensor" means Kivo. "Mod" means the Fluorescent software, including its
source code, compiled code, shaders, documentation and supplied assets, to
the extent that the Licensor has the rights to license them. Separately
licensed third-party materials are governed by their own terms.

"Preset Data" means non-executable configuration and customization data for
Fluorescent: presets, settings, block or item overrides, linked-block
settings, and painted bloom-mask data. It includes such data created or
exported with Fluorescent and any preset data supplied by the Licensor.
It does not include the Mod's code, shader implementations, compiled files,
or underlying Minecraft or resource-pack textures, models or other assets.

2. Permissions granted without asking

Subject to this license, you may:

- Download, install and run an authorized copy of the Mod for gameplay.
  You may make copies and backups for your own use. If source is supplied,
  you may read it and compile an unmodified copy for your own use.
- Configure the Mod, use its editors, paint masks, and create, edit, import,
  export, copy and share Preset Data without obtaining the Licensor's
  permission. Preset Data may be shared on its own or as the configuration
  portion of a modpack, without bundling the Mod itself.
- Create and share screenshots, gameplay videos and streams showing the
  Mod, including monetized videos and streams, subject to any applicable
  third-party terms.
- Link to the official Fluorescent download. A modpack manifest may refer
  users or launchers to an official authorized download rather than bundle
  or rehost a copy of the Mod.

The Licensor claims no ownership of your independently created Preset Data.
This license imposes no additional restriction on sharing that data to the
extent the Licensor's rights are involved. It does not grant rights to
another creator's presets or third-party content; obtain any permissions
needed from their respective owners. Sharing Preset Data alone does not
require including this license or obtaining approval from Kivo.

